ely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $444.5M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 36% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 83% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $42.72 (margin of safety -197%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 39%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Real Estate peers: EV/EBITDA 23.4 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 26% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 2.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 14 covering analysts target $152 on average, 20% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 5% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.58).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.50x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 57%.","ROE of 6% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 2.1% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.9x net debt to EBITDA ($1.1B of cash against $35.0B of debt), with interest covered 4.3x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.7% over 3 years, 14.6% over 5 years and 14.9% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 14%).","Free cash flow has compounded 33.6% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 11.3% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.1x depreciation (3.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 96%.","It returns 3.0% a year to shareholders (3.4% in dividends).","The share count has grown 4.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 28 consecutive years, raising it 16.9% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 2,802 employees, each generates about $3.1M of revenue, 1.4x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 13.3% a year.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $2.7M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $66K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":37,"head":"Avoid: priced 197% above its fair value of $42.72.","pros":["Revenue grew 14.6%/yr over 5y","14 analysts' mean target $152 (+20%)","Returns 3.0% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 197% above fair value of $42.72","ROIC 5.1% vs WACC 8.7%","Net debt/EBITDA 4.9x","EV/EBITDA 23.4x vs sector 16.3x"],"flags":["Priced 197% above its fair value of $42.72"],"need":[],"buy_below":36.31,"vc":{"base":42.72,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":42.72,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.3946,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (39% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"PLD","date":"2026-11-06"}